# Build context for the images that build from the repository root.
#
# docker-compose.yml builds backend, kb-worker, gmail-worker,
# onboarding-worker and frontend with `context: ./`, so without this file the
# entire repository — .git, frontend/node_modules, backend/.venv, roughly 1.2 GB
# — is uploaded to the Docker daemon on every build.
#
# vroom-embedding builds from `context: ./vroom-embedding` and is therefore NOT
# covered by this file. For the same reason backend/.dockerignore and
# frontend/.dockerignore are inert — Docker only reads the one at the context
# root — so this file is where those rules have to live.
#
# Patterns are matched against paths relative to the context root, and Docker
# does not imply a leading `**/`. Anything that can appear in a subdirectory
# needs the prefix spelled out.

# ---- Version control & CI ----
.git
.github
.gitignore

# ---- Python ----
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.venv
**/venv

# ---- Node / Next.js ----
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/.pnpm-store
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# A stray frontend/pnpm-workspace.yaml lands at /app in the frontend builder
# and makes pnpm resolve the app as a workspace root, which fails `pnpm build`.
# It is gitignored, so it is invisible to git status while still reaching the
# build context — hence blocking it here explicitly.
**/pnpm-workspace.yaml

# ---- Test output ----
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage

# ---- Environment / secrets ----
# Never bake local credentials into an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# ---- Editors & OS ----
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/*.log

# ---- Local agent & tooling state ----
.claude
.kiro
.pi
.codegraph
.mcp.json

# ---- Docs & compose files (no build stage reads them) ----
docs
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
